पाप॑ f. ई॑ (later आ॑) bad, wicked, evil, inauspicious;
n. पाप॑म् & f. instr. पाप॑या (±अमुया॑ q.v.) badly, wrongly. m.
bad fellow, wretch, profligate;
 n. evil, sin, harm, trouble. शान्तं
पापम् may the sin be destroyed = heaven forbid.

(पा॑प) f. ई॑ (later आ॑) bad, wicked, evil, inauspicious;
n. पाप॑म् & f. instr. पाप॑या (±अमुया॑ q.v.) badly, wrongly. m.
bad fellow, wretch, profligate;
 n. evil, sin, harm, trouble. शान्तं
पापम् may the sin be destroyed = heaven forbid.

पापक f. ˚पिका (& ˚पकी) bad, evil;
 n. evil, wrong,
sin;
 m. wicked person, villain.

2 पापकर्मन् a. doing evil;
 m. evil-doer, sinner,
villain.

पा॑पीयंस् (compar. to पाप॑) worse off, more wretched
or miserable;
 also = prec. adj. & m.
